```text
The topology implementation constructs a node-local graph containing GPU, PCI,
CPU, NIC, and NET nodes. For network devices it consumes plugin properties such
as ``name``, ``pciPath``, ``guid``, ``speed``, ``latency``, and pointer support,
then computes paths and transport scores. The path is local to each process and
is derived from Linux/sysfs-visible device ancestry and plugin metadata.

No inspected source routine identifies a remote physical USB4 cable or infers
its internal topology from an IP interface name.
```
